---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout>

  <article>

    <h1>Click Me In Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="description">
      Effective date: August 21, 2026
    </p>

    <p class="description">
      This Privacy Policy describes how Forge70 Labs handles information
      in connection with Click Me In, our iOS metronome app.
    </p>

    <p class="description">
      Click Me In is an offline, local app. Forge70 Labs does not collect
      or transmit any personal information through the app, including
      through the optional Click Me In Pro upgrade.
    </p>

    <section>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Click Me In does not collect any personal information. The app
        does not require or support accounts or login of any kind, and
        there is no way to identify you as a user of the app.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Click Me In Pro is an optional, one-time in-app purchase. Purchases
        are processed entirely by Apple through the App Store. Forge70 Labs
        does not receive or store your name, Apple Account, payment details,
        or any other personal information about your purchase. Apple's
        handling of purchase information is governed by Apple's own privacy
        policy.
      </p>

      <p class="description">
        To unlock Pro features and restore purchases, the app uses Apple's
        StoreKit framework to confirm with Apple that the upgrade has been
        purchased on your Apple Account or shared with you through Family
        Sharing. This check is between your device and Apple; no information
        about it is sent to Forge70 Labs.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Information Apple Shares With Us</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Apple provides Forge70 Labs with aggregated sales reports through
        App Store Connect. These reports do not identify you.
      </p>

      <p class="description">
        If you have chosen to share analytics with app developers in your
        device settings, Apple may also share aggregated, anonymous usage
        and crash data (App Analytics) with Forge70 Labs. This data does not
        include personal identifiers, and Apple shares it only from users
        who opt in. You can change this choice at any time in Settings &gt;
        Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Analytics &amp; Improvements.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Data Stored On Your Device</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Click Me In stores a small set of app preferences locally on your
        device, using Apple's standard UserDefaults storage. This data
        never leaves your device and is not visible to Forge70 Labs.
        It includes:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Selected click sound</li>
        <li>Click volume</li>
        <li>Downbeat and regular-beat colors</li>
        <li>Pulse intensity</li>
        <li>Visual intensity</li>
        <li>Audio and visual feedback settings</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="description">
        If you use Click Me In Pro, the songs, sets, and gigs you create are
        also stored locally on your device. This includes song names, tempo,
        and time signature; set lists and their running order; and gig
        details such as venue and date. This data never leaves your device
        and is not visible to Forge70 Labs.
      </p>

      <p class="description">
        In the free metronome, tempo (BPM) and time signature are session
        settings only. They exist in memory while the app is open and are
        not saved unless you save them as part of a song in Click Me In Pro.
      </p>

      <p class="description">
        If you back up your device with iCloud Backup or to a computer,
        Apple includes app data, such as your preferences, songs, sets, and
        gigs, in that backup under Apple's terms. Forge70 Labs has no access
        to these backups.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Data We Do Not Collect</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Click Me In does not use the microphone or record audio. It does
        not collect device identifiers, advertising identifiers, or
        location information.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Data Transmission and Third Parties</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Click Me In makes no network requests of its own, and no data is
        transmitted to Forge70 Labs. The only exception is the App Store
        communication described under In-App Purchases, which Apple handles
        through StoreKit.
      </p>

      <p class="description">
        The app does not include its own analytics or telemetry, does not include
        advertising, and does not integrate any third-party SDKs. Forge70
        Labs does not share, sell, or otherwise disclose data to third
        parties through this app, because no data is collected or
        transmitted in the first place.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Click Me In does not knowingly collect any information from
        anyone, including children, because it does not collect personal
        information from any user.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

      <p class="description">
        If this Privacy Policy changes, the updated version will be
        posted on this page with a revised effective date.
      </p>

    </section>

    <section>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>

      <p class="description">
        Questions about this Privacy Policy or Click Me In can be sent to:
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="mailto:privacy@forge70labs.com">
          privacy@forge70labs.com
        </a>
      </p>

    </section>

  </article>

</MainLayout>
